$ MacNeal & Harder (1985), Sec. 8 - pinched cylinder with end diaphragms.
$ R = 300, L = 600, t = 3, E = 3.0e6, nu = 0.3.
$ Rigid diaphragms at both ends, two opposing radial point loads P = 1 at
$ midspan (180 deg apart).
$ Octant model (1/8 of the cylinder) exploiting all three symmetries:
$   z = 0  : midspan symmetry  (Uz = Rx = Ry = 0)
$   phi=0  : loaded line       (Uy = Rx = Rz = 0)
$   phi=90 : unloaded line     (Ux = Ry = Rz = 0)
$   z = L/2 = 300 : rigid diaphragm (Ux = Uy = Rz = 0)
$ Mesh 4x4 = 16 CQUAD4, 5x5 = 25 nodes.
$ Applied load at node 1 (under load, in octant) = P/4 = 0.25 in -X.
$ Reference radial displacement at node 1: |Ux| = 1.8248e-5.
$
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = MacNeal-Harder pinched cylinder (octant, 4x4)
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL = Two opposing radial point loads, octant model
  SPC = 1
  LOAD = 1
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
BEGIN BULK
$ ---- solver parameters ----
$ Drilling-DOF stabilisation is not part of the benchmark definition and
$ solvers default it differently (MSC/Nastran 70.5 SOL 101: 0.0; MSC.Nastran
$ 2004+ and OpenJFEM: 100.0). Pinned so the accuracy and same-deck parity
$ comparisons are parameter-exact. See validation/README.md, "PARAM,K6ROT".
PARAM,K6ROT,0.
MAT1, 1, 3.0+6, , 0.3
PSHELL, 1, 1, 3.0, 1
$ ---- grids: 5 z-stations x 5 phi-stations ----
$ Node ID = 5*j + i + 1, with i in 0..4 (z) and j in 0..4 (phi).
$ z stations: 0, 75, 150, 225, 300.
$ phi stations: 0, 22.5, 45, 67.5, 90 deg.
$ x = R cos(phi), y = R sin(phi), z = z_i.
$
